Figure 6 elucidates Nano-11's role in antigen targeting and retention. Panel A shows that migratory dendritic cells (MigDCs) exhibit the highest CD86 expression among OVA-positive myeloid cells in draining lymph nodes. Panel B provides phenotyping of OVA-positive MigDCs, suggesting preferential uptake by CD11b+ DCs and MoDCs. Panel C demonstrates Nano-11's ability to retain Alexa Fluor 647-labeled OVA at the injection site for a prolonged period, comparable to aluminum hydroxide, and significantly longer than soluble OVA alone, thereby improving antigen persistence for immune cell interaction.